This is my second acension so I was pretty proud that it was a tourist.
Once I found a 2-handed sword and got to basic I didn't have very many
problems this game. First acension was just posted recently.

Was thinking about trying to do it wishless but then I found a magic
lamp in minetown and decided that I just absolutely needed to get
Grayswandir. Decided that I would definately go polyless and genoless
if I didn't get into too big of trouble. Found amulet in sokobon and by
this time was really starting to get weighed down with stuff. Got
another wish somewhere before castle that I used on BoH. Did Ludius w/o
=oC without any problems and wound up with yellow DSM that got
enchanted up to +4 before I swapped for SDSM. Did protection down to a
naked -2ac. Went on a sac-fest, got Vorpy and got crowned way too
early. Can anyone give me a tip on the method to convince the gods to
give me more gifts? Do you just keep sac'ing w/o praying? or do you sac
until you see the clover and then pray?

Went down to castle before I did quest since my level was high enough
yet. Saw a Ki-rin in castle that I wound up teleporting into one of the
shops and since I had found a spellbook of charm monster I left it in
there until I could charm him.

I had a decent kit at this point (AoR, Cloak of MR, YDSM, GoDex) but I
decided since PYEC gave me MR I would ditch the amulet, get the SDSM,
Oilskin cloak for those nasty swimmers, speed boots, Helm of
Brilliance, marker and an archon for a pet. Don Vito shows up with a
sunsword (never picked it up so I guess the game didn't register that I
saw it; how could I not!!).  At this point I was thinking about time
for YASD. Don Vito was ridiculous. I never bothered to enchant any of
his stuff but by the time I got to the planes he was level 32, with
~240hp -12AC but unfortunately, I left him behind after hanging out for
like 50k turns with him.

So I went back and did the Quest, accidentally did something to tick
off two of the guides so I slept them until I could finish the quest.
Wound up spending a LOT of time on this quest sifting through all the
monsters and eq in the shops. Reaffirmed that I didn't want to polypile
anything. I actually never found a wand of poly so I consider myself
lucky to not be tempted. Finished the quest and realized how absolutely
cool the PYEC is. Quickly blew up a ring of increase damage...got the
second one to +7. Later I blew up another and was able to get another
one to +3 right at the end.

For a while I was 2-weaponing with katana but found silver saber on
minetown captain. After a while of collecting elven daggers, I
enchanted a bunch up to +6 which I started using on MF and MMF.

Went back and charmed my Ki-rin named Karen. Had a saddle from some
shop earlier and wound up riding her from this point on. Once I got
basic it was a treat. Side note: If I am on a flying steed but have
basic riding skill I can pick stuff up off ground. Yet then I put on my
=oL and I stay riding but can no longer get stuff off ground? IMO: you
should not be able to pick stuff off ground from a flying steed unless
you are Skilled or higher, or perhaps you should float off your steed
if you put on =oL or BoL.

Gehennom was not bad (magic mapping on VotD priest.) One point in
Gehennom both pets got level ported to about DL12 so I went up, tracked
em down and recharmed them both. Yay. Decided to kill Asmodeus and
Baalzebub, but no desire to see Demogorgon (I think my next goal may be
to kill that in another game). Orcus died quickly and wound up going
all the way down to vibrating square before I realized I hadn't found
Vlad yet. Did find a second WoW in Orcustown that I used 3 wishes on
and exited with two remaining. Used one on another marker, one on a
T-shirt when I accidentally read ?ofDestroy Armor when a MMF helped me
forget that scroll and forget last one. Back up again, did that and got
started on Rodney. Those two pets, MM, and oilskin cloak made the moat
monsters less scary. Rodney gave up the goods on first /oD shot. Saw
him again in the sanctum where it took 2 shots. May I say again how
cool PYEC is; especially when you arent polypiling. Twice I had liches
summon MMF right next to me. Very annoying to have to re'id half your
stuff.

On the way back up RNG didn't like me as I went up the stairs. Must
have lost about 25 levels between 48 and 43. All of these were where
the stairs were not close at all. Once I got up to about DL 38 I had no
problems, thank goodness those stairs were all about 10 spaces apart.
With only 100 Pw, I had a hard time casting much while carrying the
AoY, even though I had a lot of good spells that I could cast at 0%
failure.

Had only two scrolls of gold detection, killed Rodney again on earth.
At this point I had 5 AoLS (and one on archon). And I almost wound up
using one on plane of air. Got so excited that I forgot to eat and
fainted as another archon surrounded me with nasties. Karen died while
I sat slumped over in the saddle. Perhaps the jolt from hitting the
ground woke me. I think I was down to about 40hp before I turned the
tide. Was fortunate in plane of fire that I found the portal quickly
and then wound up losing Don Vito when I stumbled into portal on plane
of water with him 2 squares away. A leash at that point might have
helped.

Never was challenged in astral plane with my +7 Grayswandir / +7 silver
saber / +7 ring of damage and 10 +6 elven daggers (expert). I could
kill the riders with either a double melee shot or about 3-4 daggers.
Yikes. Let another lich summon in some more nasties and then charmed a
bunch right before heading off into the sunset. Managed to exit with a
lot of gems, several AoLS, my original Leica camera, Vorpy, and three
Nazgul rings. Starting to work on the style points now too. :)

